x86_64-linux  the Itanium tables cxx1 writes for the host targets carry no must-not-throw region over a cleanup pad, so the throw from ~Loud unwinds like a fresh exception and the handler catches 2 where the standard says terminate; the C6000 table has the scope (cl6x's catch-and-terminate over the pad), and this case measures that target. The host half is a gap of its own.
x86_64-windows  the same gap, in the Microsoft tables' terms: no funclet is marked to terminate.
arm64-darwin  the same gap as x86_64-linux.
